**Read:** Revisit the passages used in the three investigations. Continue with the full NASA, LBNL, WHO and air-cleaning readings as their deeper physical and operational questions arise.

Explain the chain from useful function to unwanted material, transfer, sample, measurement and conclusion. Keep number, mass, surface area, film thickness and biological evidence distinct. Show how time, operating state and sampling conditions can change the meaning of a result.

**Work:** Present your three investigations to a reader who did not choose their assumptions. Defend the units and balances, recompute one result independently and revise an inference after a reasonable challenge. Identify the observations still needed to design or qualify the actual process.

The next depth concerns particle and molecular transport, surface interactions, filtration, airflow, facility construction, cleaning, utilities, monitoring, operation and specialist manufacturing investigations. These foundations give those choices physical meaning; they do not make a facility qualified by themselves.

